.SH AGENTS
duscope serves AI agents with the verbs and flags people use and one JSON
envelope.
Run by an agent's client, which it tells by
.BR CLAUDECODE ,
.BR CODEX_THREAD_ID ,
.B CODEX_VERSION
or
.BR GEMINI_CLI ,
a verb writes JSON unless a flag or
.B DUSCOPE_FORMAT
asks for another format; outside a terminal and an agent's client it
writes
.BR plain .
.SS "The briefing"
.B duscope agent
prints, as Markdown on stdout, the briefing an agent reads before it uses
duscope: what duscope never does, which verb answers which question, the
handle that
.B explain
issues and
.B clean
checks, the exit codes and error codes, and the tables
.B query \-\-sql
reads.
The verbs, codes and schema version in it are the running binary's own.
.SS "The skill"
.B duscope agent \-\-skill
writes the briefing as a skill, which an agent's client loads by itself
when a question calls for it:
.I SKILL.md
and
.I references/sql.md
in
.I .agents/skills/duscope/
and
.I .claude/skills/duscope/
under the working directory or
.BR \-\-dir .
A skill already there is replaced only with
.BR \-\-force .
.PP
The skill is recommended.
In the project's evaluation, 120 runs of ten disk\-hygiene tasks through
Claude Code, agents completed every task with it and without it, and with
it used 29.5% fewer tokens and about two turns fewer a run; it is
described in
.IR bench/README.md ,
in the source distribution.
